  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Mouse Aiming**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the codebase related to mouse aiming. Specifically, I\'m meticulously examining the `InputManager`, `FlightController`, `MouseResponseCurve`, `steering`, and `Camera` files to understand the entire pipeline. I am tracing the input events and processing logic to find any flaws in the aiming system.\n\n\n**Investigating Missing Params**\n\nI\'ve discovered a discrepancy! `InputManager.ts` references parameters like `stickSelfCenterRate` and `maxStickDeflection` within `STEERING_CONFIG`, but these variables are absent from the `steering.ts` file itself. I\'m now investigating where these parameters are defined, or, if they are even defined and passed from elsewhere to the input manager, and, if not, why the code compiles without obvious errors. I\'m focusing on the call to `input.consumeSnapshot(dt, settings)` in `GameScene.tsx` to understand the flow of these settings.\n\n\n"
