  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Angular Velocities**\n\nI\'ve been calculating angular velocities based on pixel movements per frame, specifically at 60 FPS. I\'ve determined that 1 pixel per frame translates to 0.0077 degrees per frame, or 0.46 degrees per second. A 2-pixel movement per frame is equivalent to 0.0184 degrees per frame, or 1.10 degrees per second. I\'m expanding this with further calculations.\n\n\n**Calculating Complex Maneuvers**\n\nI\'ve determined that a movement of 3.5 pixels/frame results in a tracking rate of 2.481\302\260/s. I\'ve also analyzed a scenario of repeated small corrections. Four cycles of +3px then -3px corrections around a fixed point resulted in zero drift and oscillation, returning precisely to 0.0000\302\260. Finally, I evaluated stopping on an enemy. Post-stop, the heading, aim ray yaw, and yaw velocity are all 0.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "ij__apXVK5W3sOIP9favqQs"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_17525128039533141360"
