  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. Root Cause of Aiming Overshoot\n\nTracing the end-to-end flight control pipeline (`InputManager` $\\rightarrow$ `MouseResponseCurve` $\\rightarrow$ `FlightController` $\\rightarrow$ `CameraController` $\\rightarrow$ `CombatManager` HUD projection) revealed four concrete causes of aiming overshoot:\n\n1. **Velocity-Coupled Gimbal & Boresight Snap-Back (`FlightController.getAimDirectionWorld`)**:\n   - In `direct-nonlinear` mode, `this.aimCursorX` and `this.aimCursorY` are driven by the ship\'s **instantaneous angular velocity** (`-this.yawVelocity / effectiveMaxYaw`) and decay back to `0` whenever mouse movement stops.\n   - However, `getAimDirectionWorld()` was still applying the virtual-joystick positional gimbal offset (`aimCursorX * 0.22 rad` = **`12.6\302\260` yaw**, `aimCursorY * 0.16 rad` = **`9.2\302\260` pitch**) on top of the ship\'s quaternion rotation.\n   - As a result, while the mouse was moving, the projected 3D boresight reticle (`boresightScreenX`, `boresightScreenY`) jumped ahead of the ship\'s actual nose proportional to mouse velocity; then, **the instant the player stopped moving the mouse on an enemy**, `yawVelocity` dropped to `0` and `aimCursorX` decayed back to `0`, causing the aiming reticle to **snap backward off the target** after the mouse had already stopped. During repeated left/right counter-corrections, this velocity-driven gimbal whipped across the nose in both directions.\n2. **Excessive Center Slope & Small-Input Gain (`DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG`)**:\n   - In `g(u) = a * u + (1 - a) * u^p`, `precisionLinearBlend` (`a = 0.25`) forced the minimum slope at the center (`u = 0`) to 25% of full linear speed, while `responseCurve` (`p = 1.85`) and `inputNormalizationRange` (`1600 px/s`) ramped up too quickly across fine corrective movements (`2\342\200\2238 px/frame` at 60 FPS).\n   - Combined with `maxYawRate = 3.5 rad/s` (`200.5\302\260/s`, 67% above the Interceptor\'s base `yawSpeed = 2.1 rad/s`), a small `4 px/frame` correction produced **`12.0\302\260/s`** of rotation and an `8 px/frame` corrective flick produced **`31.3\302\260/s`** (`3.1\302\260` in 100 ms \342\200\224 more than double an enemy fighter\'s `~1.5\302\260` angular silhouette at 250 m).\n3. **Opposite-Direction Residual Velocity on Reversal (`stepDirectAngularRate`)**:\n   - When rapidly reversing mouse direction (`targetRate * currentRate < 0`) during a counter-correction, exponential smoothing blended from the old opposite-sign `currentRate` rather than zero-crossing immediately, introducing phase lag that encouraged over-correction.\n4. **Missing Baseline Stick Bounds in `steering.ts` / `InputManager.ts`**:\n   - `InputManager.consumeSnapshot` referenced `STEERING_CONFIG.stickSelfCenterRate`, `STEERING_CONFIG.maxStickDeflection`, and `STEERING_CONFIG.baseMouseSensitivity`, which had been omitted from `steering.ts`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Exact Parameters and Functions Changed\n\n- **Nonlinear Steering Calibration (`DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG` in `src/config/steering.ts`)**:\n  - `precisionLinearBlend`: `0.25` $\\rightarrow$ **`0.08`** (reduces center linear floor slope by 68% while avoiding a deadzone).\n  - `responseCurve`: `1.85` $\\rightarrow$ **`2.25`** (flattens the fine-aim region for micro-corrections while ramping smoothly into medium and large turns).\n  - `inputNormalizationRange`: `1600` $\\rightarrow$ **`1800` px/s** (`30 px/frame` at 60 FPS).\n  - `maxYawRate`: `3.5` $\\rightarrow$ **`2.6` rad/s** (`~149\302\260/s`).\n  - `maxPitchRate`: `3.0` $\\rightarrow$ **`2.25` rad/s** (`~129\302\260/s`).\n  - `inputSmoothing`: `0.08` $\\rightarrow$ **`0.04`** (`tau = 2 ms`).\n  - `stopDecayMultiplier`: `2.5` $\\rightarrow$ **`4.5`**.\n  - Restored `baseMouseSensitivity`, `stickSelfCenterRate`, and `maxStickDeflection` to `BASELINE_STEERING_CONFIG`, `STEERING_CONFIG`, and `STEERING_BOUNDS` (and marked `stickSelfCenterRate` / `maxStickDeflection` optional on `VirtualStickParams` in `src/engine/InputManager.ts`).\n- **Zero-Reversal-Lag & Instant Stop (`stepDirectAngularRate` in `src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`)**:\n  - Resets `baseCurrent` to `0` on sign reversal (`targetRate * currentRate < 0`) so counter-corrections respond immediately in the new direction on the first frame without fighting leftover opposite-sign angular velocity.\n  - Snaps stopping decay `< 0.02 rad/s` immediately to `0` so stopping the mouse leaves zero coasting angular momentum.\n- **True Boresight Alignment & Reticle Settling (`getAimDirectionWorld` and `update` in `src/engine/FlightController.ts`)**:\n  - In `direct-nonlinear` mode, `getAimDirectionWorld()` now aligns directly with the ship\'s true forward vector (`_FORWARD_LOCAL`) instead of applying the velocity-driven `GIMBAL_MAX_YAW_RAD` / `GIMBAL_MAX_PITCH_RAD` offset (which remains preserved for `virtual-joystick-baseline` rollback).\n  - Increased HUD turn-indicator stop-settling rate to `42.0` (`0.5 px` snap threshold) when mouse input ceases.\n- **Settings Migration (`src/config/ships.ts`)**:\n  - Bumped `SETTINGS_STORAGE_KEY` to `\'starfall.settings.v8\'` (with automatic fallback migration from `v7` and earlier) so existing browser sessions receive the calibrated steering defaults while keeping user graphics, audio, camera, `joystickRadius`, and `invertY` preferences.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Why the Changes Improve Fine Aiming & Preserve Large-Turn Capability\n\n- **3.9x\342\200\2234.8x Finer Micro-Aim Precision**:\n  - At 60 FPS, a `1 px/frame` nudge now rotates the ship by **`0.0077\302\260/frame`** (`0.46\302\260/s`, down from `2.23\302\260/s`), a `2 px/frame` correction rotates by **`0.0184\302\260/frame`** (`1.10\302\260/s`, down from `5.01\302\260/s`), and a `4 px/frame` adjustment rotates by **`0.0510\302\260/frame`** (`3.06\302\260/s`, down from `12.01\302\260/s`).\n- **Zero Post-Stop Reticle Snap-Back**:\n  - Aligning `getAimDirectionWorld()` with the ship\'s true boresight in `direct-nonlinear` mode ensures that when the player stops the mouse on an enemy, both ship rotation and the projected 3D aiming crosshair stop dead-on the target with `0.0000\302\260` of post-stop snap-back.\n- **Large-Turn Capability Preserved**:\n  - Base `mouseSensitivity` remains **`1.0x`**.\n  - Because `g(u) = 0.08 * u + 0.92 * u^2.25` anchors at `g(1.0) = 1.0` and soft-saturates smoothly above `knee = 0.85`, a brisk `30 px/frame` (`1800 px/s`) swipe commands **`143.6\302\260/s`** of yaw and a `45 px/frame` swipe commands **`149.0\302\260/s`** (`2.6 rad/s`, turning 90\302\260 in `0.60 s` and 180\302\260 in `1.20 s`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Validation & Test Results\n\nAll six required scenarios were verified quantitatively through deterministic 60 FPS engine + 3D camera projection simulations:\n\n1. **Tiny left/right corrections (`1 px`, `2 px`, `4 px` per frame)**:\n   - Produced `0.0077\302\260`, `0.0184\302\260`, and `0.0510\302\260` per frame respectively \342\200\224 smooth, continuous, and sub-degree controllable.\n2. **Repeated small corrections around a fixed point (`+3 px` for 6 frames, `-3 px` for 6 frames across 4 cycles)**:\n   - Cycled cleanly between `+0.1962\302\260` and `0.0000\302\260` on every cycle (`[0.1962\302\260, 0.0000\302\260, 0.1962\302\260, 0.0000\302\260, 0.1962\302\260, 0.0000\302\260, 0.1962\302\260, 0.0000\302\260]`) with zero drift or oscillation buildup.\n3. **Slowly tracking a moving enemy (`3.5 px/frame` sustained for `1.0 s`)**:\n   - Maintained a steady, predictable `2.481\302\260/s` tracking rate (`2.481\302\260` over 60 frames).\n4. **Stopping the reticle on an enemy (`10 px/frame` slew followed by `0 px` hold)**:\n   - Heading at stop: `3.1086\302\260`; heading 10 frames after stop: `3.1086\302\260` (**`0.000000\302\260` post-stop heading overshoot**).\n   - Boresight aim ray at stop: `3.1086\302\260`; boresight aim ray 10 frames after stop: `3.1086\302\260` (**`0.000000\302\260` post-stop snap-back**).\n   - `yawVelocity` on the first frame of zero input: **`0 rad/s`**.\n5. **Rapidly reversing steering direction (`+14 px/frame` right turn $\\rightarrow$ `-6 px/frame` left counter-correction)**:\n   - Angular velocity reversed sign on the very first reversal frame (`-0.5276 rad/s` $\\rightarrow$ `+0.1056 rad/s`), immediately moving heading `-0.1008\302\260` in the counter-correction direction with zero opposite-direction coasting.\n6. **Large directional turns (`30 px/frame` and `45 px/frame` for `1.0 s`)**:\n   - Reached **`143.64\302\260/s`** at `30 px/frame` and **`148.97\302\260/s`** at `45 px/frame`.\n\n**Browser Testing Limitation Note**: A local headless/GUI browser binary (Chromium/Chrome) and physical mouse hardware are not installed in this container environment, so validation was performed via 60 FPS runtime simulation of `FlightController`, `MouseResponseCurve`, `CameraController`, and `CombatManager` 3D-to-screen projection rather than physical mouse hardware in a live browser window."
    message_id: "2T__apXRGMmd_uMPk_P2oAg"
    modified_response: "### 1. Root Cause of Aiming Overshoot\n\nTracing the end-to-end flight control pipeline (`InputManager` $\\rightarrow$ `MouseResponseCurve` $\\rightarrow$ `FlightController` $\\rightarrow$ `CameraController` $\\rightarrow$ `CombatManager` HUD projection) revealed four concrete causes of aiming overshoot:\n\n1. **Velocity-Coupled Gimbal & Boresight Snap-Back (`FlightController.getAimDirectionWorld`)**:\n   - In `direct-nonlinear` mode, `this.aimCursorX` and `this.aimCursorY` are driven by the ship\'s **instantaneous angular velocity** (`-this.yawVelocity / effectiveMaxYaw`) and decay back to `0` whenever mouse movement stops.\n   - However, `getAimDirectionWorld()` was still applying the virtual-joystick positional gimbal offset (`aimCursorX * 0.22 rad` = **`12.6\302\260` yaw**, `aimCursorY * 0.16 rad` = **`9.2\302\260` pitch**) on top of the ship\'s quaternion rotation.\n   - As a result, while the mouse was moving, the projected 3D boresight reticle (`boresightScreenX`, `boresightScreenY`) jumped ahead of the ship\'s actual nose proportional to mouse velocity; then, **the instant the player stopped moving the mouse on an enemy**, `yawVelocity` dropped to `0` and `aimCursorX` decayed back to `0`, causing the aiming reticle to **snap backward off the target** after the mouse had already stopped. During repeated left/right counter-corrections, this velocity-driven gimbal whipped across the nose in both directions.\n2. **Excessive Center Slope & Small-Input Gain (`DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG`)**:\n   - In `g(u) = a * u + (1 - a) * u^p`, `precisionLinearBlend` (`a = 0.25`) forced the minimum slope at the center (`u = 0`) to 25% of full linear speed, while `responseCurve` (`p = 1.85`) and `inputNormalizationRange` (`1600 px/s`) ramped up too quickly across fine corrective movements (`2\342\200\2238 px/frame` at 60 FPS).\n   - Combined with `maxYawRate = 3.5 rad/s` (`200.5\302\260/s`, 67% above the Interceptor\'s base `yawSpeed = 2.1 rad/s`), a small `4 px/frame` correction produced **`12.0\302\260/s`** of rotation and an `8 px/frame` corrective flick produced **`31.3\302\260/s`** (`3.1\302\260` in 100 ms \342\200\224 more than double an enemy fighter\'s `~1.5\302\260` angular silhouette at 250 m).\n3. **Opposite-Direction Residual Velocity on Reversal (`stepDirectAngularRate`)**:\n   - When rapidly reversing mouse direction (`targetRate * currentRate < 0`) during a counter-correction, exponential smoothing blended from the old opposite-sign `currentRate` rather than zero-crossing immediately, introducing phase lag that encouraged over-correction.\n4. **Missing Baseline Stick Bounds in `steering.ts` / `InputManager.ts`**:\n   - `InputManager.consumeSnapshot` referenced `STEERING_CONFIG.stickSelfCenterRate`, `STEERING_CONFIG.maxStickDeflection`, and `STEERING_CONFIG.baseMouseSensitivity`, which had been omitted from `steering.ts`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Exact Parameters and Functions Changed\n\n- **Nonlinear Steering Calibration (`DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG` in `src/config/steering.ts`)**:\n  - `precisionLinearBlend`: `0.25` $\\rightarrow$ **`0.08`** (reduces center linear floor slope by 68% while avoiding a deadzone).\n  - `responseCurve`: `1.85` $\\rightarrow$ **`2.25`** (flattens the fine-aim region for micro-corrections while ramping smoothly into medium and large turns).\n  - `inputNormalizationRange`: `1600` $\\rightarrow$ **`1800` px/s** (`30 px/frame` at 60 FPS).\n  - `maxYawRate`: `3.5` $\\rightarrow$ **`2.6` rad/s** (`~149\302\260/s`).\n  - `maxPitchRate`: `3.0` $\\rightarrow$ **`2.25` rad/s** (`~129\302\260/s`).\n  - `inputSmoothing`: `0.08` $\\rightarrow$ **`0.04`** (`tau = 2 ms`).\n  - `stopDecayMultiplier`: `2.5` $\\rightarrow$ **`4.5`**.\n  - Restored `baseMouseSensitivity`, `stickSelfCenterRate`, and `maxStickDeflection` to `BASELINE_STEERING_CONFIG`, `STEERING_CONFIG`, and `STEERING_BOUNDS` (and marked `stickSelfCenterRate` / `maxStickDeflection` optional on `VirtualStickParams` in `src/engine/In