  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Report Details**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the user\'s bug report, specifically focusing on the observed behavior: the reticle\'s abrupt \"snap\" or rebound at the aim boundary. This testing context reveals an important clue, hopefully illuminating the core issue at hand.\n\n\n**Refining Input Handling**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got it. The root cause is that the current design forces reticle recentering at the aim boundary, hindering smooth steering. The user\'s input demands that I remove this behavior. It seems the reticle should just visually clamp. Moving outward must still steer, and opposite movement must reduce steering. No more snaps!\n\n\n"
