    thinking: "**Analyzing Chromium Performance**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the live Chromium browser results from task 75, and I\'m quite pleased. Every single test shows 100% success. Notably, the \"Slowly move reticle to boundary\" test is behaving exactly as expected, which suggests the underlying logic is sound.\n\n\n\n**Observing Boundary Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the reticle\'s behavior past the boundary. It appears clamped, and continues turning without interruption, even beyond the initial boundary point. I\'ve noted the consistent values for `joystickX`, `aimScreenX`, and `domScreenX`, along with the `yawVelocity` and `headingDeg` data in several frames. This suggests predictable behavior extending beyond the limit.\n\n\n**Examining Reticle Response**\n\nI\'m now investigating the reticle\'s behavior when reversing mouse direction from the boundary and performing large directional turns. The reticle moved inward and the yaw reversed immediately on the first frame of the reverse test. The max turn speed is reached when performing a large turn. When the mouse stops, the reticle stays clamped at the boundary.\n\n\n"
