  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. Exact Recentering Logic Removed or Modified\n\n1. **`src/engine/FlightController.ts` (`FlightController.update` \342\200\224 `direct-nonlinear` mode)**:\n   - **Removed** the velocity-coupled spring-return recentering logic that previously tied the visual reticle position `(this.joystickX, this.joystickY)` to instantaneous angular velocity and pulled it back toward `(0, 0)` every frame:\n     ```ts\n     // REMOVED:\n     const desiredReticleX = normTurnX * this.aimBoundary.halfW;\n     const desiredReticleY = normTurnY * this.aimBoundary.halfH;\n     const isReticleStopping = desiredReticleX === 0 && desiredReticleY === 0;\n     const reticleRate = isReticleStopping ? 42.0 : 22.0;\n     const reticleAlpha = 1 - Math.exp(-reticleRate * safeDt);\n     this.joystickX += (desiredReticleX - this.joystickX) * reticleAlpha;\n     this.joystickY += (desiredReticleY - this.joystickY) * reticleAlpha;\n     if (desiredReticleX === 0 && Math.abs(this.joystickX) < 0.5) this.joystickX = 0;\n     if (desiredReticleY === 0 && Math.abs(this.joystickY) < 0.5) this.joystickY = 0;\n     ```\n   - **Replaced** with direct accumulation of relative mouse movement `(input.mouseDeltaX, input.mouseDeltaY)` onto `(this.joystickX, this.joystickY)` followed by `clampToRoundedRect(candidateX, candidateY, this.aimBoundary, this.aimClamp)`:\n     - The visual reticle moves naturally with mouse input and clamps smoothly onto the rounded-rectangle aim boundary perimeter without snapping, bouncing, or springing back to the center.\n     - Steering demand (`evaluateDirectMouseSteering`) continues evaluating raw Pointer Lock deltas `(input.mouseDeltaX, input.mouseDeltaY)` independently of the clamped visual reticle coordinates, so outward mouse movement past the boundary continues turning the ship without interruption and reversing mouse direction immediately moves the reticle inward while reversing steering demand.\n\n2. **`src/engine/InputManager.ts` (`InputManager.consumeSnapshot`)**:\n   - **Removed** the per-frame exponential self-centering decay (`this.stickX *= halfDecay; this.stickY *= halfDecay;`) while Pointer Lock is active (`lockOwned === true`), so internal stick state also never forces automatic recentering while the player is steering.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Relevant Files Changed\n\n- `src/engine/FlightController.ts`\n- `src/engine/InputManager.ts`\n\n*(Global sensitivity, maximum turn rates, fine-aiming response curve parameters, Pointer Lock, camera, and HUD layout were preserved unchanged.)*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Live Chromium Browser Validation Results\n\nTested in a live Chromium browser (`1280\303\227720` viewport, right aim boundary at `+192 px` / `screenX = 0.6500`) against the running app on port 3000 by launching Campaign Mission 01, engaging Pointer Lock on the WebGL canvas, dispatching real `MouseEvent(\'mousemove\', { movementX, movementY })` events across animation frames, and verifying both live DOM attributes on `[data-testid=\"virtual-mouse-cursor\"]` and runtime flight telemetry:\n\n1. **Slowly move the reticle toward the boundary (`+16 px/frame` for 12 frames)**:\n   - Frame 1: `joystickX = 16 px`, `domScreenX = 0.5125`, `domZone = \"active\"`, `headingDeg = 0.247\302\260`\n   - Frame 6: `joystickX = 96 px`, `domScreenX = 0.5750`, `domZone = \"active\"`, `headingDeg = 2.392\302\260`\n   - Frame 12: `joystickX = 192 px`, `domScreenX = 0.6500`, `domZone = \"max\"`, `headingDeg = 4.815\302\260`\n   - Reticle moved smoothly to the boundary with zero snap or rebound.\n2. **Continue moving outward after reaching the boundary (`+20 px/frame` for 10 additional frames) & 3. Verify uninterrupted turning**:\n   - Frame 1 past boundary: `joystickX = 192 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6500`, `domZone = \"max\"`), `yawVelocity = -0.1273 rad/s`, `headingDeg = 5.179\302\260`\n   - Frame 5 past boundary: `joystickX = 192 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6500`, `domZone = \"max\"`), `yawVelocity = -0.1273 rad/s`, `headingDeg = 6.638\302\260`\n   - Frame 10 past boundary: `joystickX = 192 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6500`, `domZone = \"max\"`), `yawVelocity = -0.1273 rad/s`, `headingDeg = 8.462\302\260`\n   - `clampedAtBoundaryEveryFrame: true`, `uninterruptedTurningEveryFrame: true`.\n4. **Reverse mouse direction from the boundary (`-18 px/frame` for 6 frames)**:\n   - Frame 1 after reversal: `joystickX = 174 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6359`), `yawVelocity = +0.1056 rad/s`, `headingDeg = 8.160\302\260`\n   - Frame 3 after reversal: `joystickX = 138 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6078`), `yawVelocity = +0.1056 rad/s`, `headingDeg = 7.555\302\260`\n   - Frame 6 after reversal: `joystickX = 84 px` (`domScreenX = 0.5656`), `yawVelocity = +0.1056 rad/s`, `headingDeg = 6.647\302\260`\n   - `reticleMovedInwardImmediatelyOnFrame1: true`, `yawReversedImmediatelyOnFrame1: true` (zero dead travel or unwind delay).\n5. **Perform a large directional turn (`+32 px/frame` for 20 frames)**:\n   - Heading rotated continuously from `7.528\302\260` to `29.066\302\260` at peak yaw rate `-2.5999 rad/s` (`~149\302\260/s`) while the reticle remained visually clamped at `192 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6500`).\n6. **Stop moving the mouse at the boundary (`0 px/frame` for 10 frames)**:\n   - Frame 1 after stop: `joystickX = 192 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6500`), `yawVelocity = 0`, `headingDeg = 29.066\302\260`\n   - Frame 10 after stop: `joystickX = 192 px` (`domScreenX = 0.6500`), `yawVelocity = 0`, `headingDeg = 29.066\302\260`\n   - `zeroHeadingDrift: true`, `zeroYawVelocity: true`, `reticleStayedAtBoundaryWithoutRecenter: true`."
