  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: Fix continuous mouse steering beyond the aim boundary in **STARFALL** (`# STARFALL \342\200\224 Critical Fix: Continuous Steering Beyond Aim Boundary`).\n- **Observed User Failure**:\n  - The forced reticle rebound was removed in the prior turn, so the visual reticle stays clamped at the aim boundary.\n  - However, when the reticle reaches the aim boundary during real gameplay, the ship stops turning (or barely turns), forcing the player to repeatedly flick/move the mouse to produce intermittent turning.\n- **Required Architecture & Success Criteria**:\n  - Cleanly separate three independent values:\n    1. `mouseDelta`: raw Pointer Lock relative mouse movement (`movementX`, `movementY`), processed exactly once per frame and never discarded when the reticle reaches its visual boundary.\n    2. `reticlePosition`: bounded visual HUD position (`joystickX`, `joystickY` $\\rightarrow$ `aimScreenX`, `aimScreenY`), clamped to the rounded-rectangle aim boundary without bouncing, resetting, or auto-recentering, and never used as the sole source of steering input.\n    3. `steeringDemand`: continuous flight-control input (`steerYaw`, `steerPitch`, `targetYawRate`, `targetPitchRate`), converted directly from raw mouse movement independently of the clamped visual reticle.\n  - Expected behavior:\n    - Continuous rightward/leftward/vertical mouse movement produces continuous, uninterrupted rightward/leftward/pitch steering before, at, and beyond the visual aim boundary.\n    - Reversing mouse direction without lifting or repositioning the mouse immediately and smoothly reverses steering demand.\n    - Stopping mouse movement stops adding new steering demand (no artificial angular inertia or new virtual joystick).\n    - Fine-aiming response curve preserved where possible.\n- **Scope Boundaries & Strict Preservation**:\n  - Do NOT modify: Pointer Lock implementation, physical mouse-edge continuity fix, existing sensitivity settings (`mouseSensitivity: 1.0`, `yawRate: 1.0`, `pitchRate: 0.9`), maximum yaw/pitch rates (`maxYawRate: 2.6`, `maxPitchRate: 2.25`), `CameraController`, combat/weapon systems, or HUD layout.\n  - Do NOT rewrite `FlightController` or merely increase the aim boundary size.\n- **Required Validation & Deliverables**:\n  - Run all 7 acceptance tests in a live browser (Playwright Chromium against `http://localhost:3000`):\n    1. Hold continuous mouse movement in one direction for several seconds.\n    2. Reach the reticle boundary and continue moving the mouse.\n    3. Verify uninterrupted ship rotation.\n    4. Reverse mouse direction without lifting or repositioning the mouse.\n    5. Verify continuous steering reversal.\n    6. Repeat vertically for pitch.\n    7. Verify the reticle stays visually bounded without interrupting flight control.\n  - Report the exact root cause and code changes, and clearly distinguish automated simulation / Playwright testing from physical-mouse gameplay verification.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Earlier Turns**:\n  - Turn 1: Reduced fine-aiming overshoot in `/src/config/steering.ts`, `/src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`, `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `/src/engine/InputManager.ts`, and `/src/config/ships.ts` (aligned `getAimDirectionWorld` with `_FORWARD_LOCAL` in `direct-nonlinear` mode to eliminate velocity-driven gimbal snap-back; restored missing `stickSelfCenterRate`, `maxStickDeflection`, `baseMouseSensitivity` properties in `steering.ts` to fix `tsc --noEmit` errors).\n  - Turn 2: Removed velocity-coupled spring recentering (`desiredReticleX = normTurnX * halfW`) from `/src/engine/FlightController.ts` and active-lock `halfDecay` from `/src/engine/InputManager.ts`, replacing reticle updates with `candidateX = this.joystickX + input.mouseDeltaX * inputScale` clamped via `clampToRoundedRect`, and restarted the dev server (`restart_dev_server`).\n- **Inspected / Analyzed in Current Turn (Turn 3 \342\200\224 Not Yet Edited)**:\n  - Read `/src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx`, `/src/config/steering.ts`, `/src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`, and `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`.\n  - Diagnosed the exact root causes of why continuous mouse movement stalls when the reticle reaches the boundary in real browser gameplay.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Root Cause Diagnosis\nWhy the ship stops turning when the reticle reaches the aim boundary during real human gameplay (requiring repeated mouse flicks for intermittent turning):\n\n1. **Mismatch Between Visual Reticle Travel Rate and `inputNormalizationRange` (`1800 px/s`) During Continuous Multi-Second Mouse Movement**:\n   - In `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`, the visual reticle accumulates `input.mouseDeltaX * inputScale` (`1.0 px/px` at 720p, `1.5 px/px` at 1080p), reaching the `192 px` aim boundary after only `192 px` of mouse travel (`~0.3\342\200\2230.6 seconds`).\n   - However, when a human player holds continuous mouse movement in one direction for **several seconds** on a physical mousepad without lifting the mouse (Acceptance Tests 1\342\200\2234), their sustainable physical hand glide speed is **`200\342\200\223600 CSS px/s`** (`3.3\342\200\22310 px/frame` at 60 FPS).\n   - Because `DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG.inputNormalizationRange` was set to **`1800 px/s`** (`30 px/frame` at 60 FPS \342\200\224 a high-speed wrist flick that travels 67 inches in 3 seconds!) with `responseCurve = 2.25` and `precisionLinearBlend = 0.08`:\n     - A continuous multi-second glide of `200\342\200\223350 px/s` produces `u = 0.11..0.19`, where `g(u) = 0.014..0.036` (**1.4% to 3.6% of max turn rate** = only **`2.1\302\260/s to 5.3\302\260/s`**!).\n     - Thus, during the first `192 px` (`~0.5s`), the player sees the reticle rapidly cross the screen and hit the aim boundary while the ship turns only `~2\302\260\342\200\2233\302\260`. Once the reticle clamps at the boundary and stops moving visually, continuing to glide the mouse at `200\342\200\223350 px/s` turns the ship at only `2\302\260/s\342\200\2235\302\260/s` (visually frozen!).\n     - To achieve meaningful turn rates (`60\302\260/s\342\200\223149\302\260/s`), the player was forced to repeatedly flick/whip the mouse above `1200\342\200\2231800 px/s`, producing intermittent bursts of rotation on each flick.\n\n2. **Single-Frame Browser Event Coalescing Dropouts (`stepDirectAngularRate` in `/src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`)**:\n   - In real browsers (especially on 120Hz/144Hz displays or when browser `mousemove` dispatch cadence doesn\'t align 1:1 with every `requestAnimationFrame` tick during a steady continuous drag), isolated render frames occur where `input.mouseDeltaX === 0` for 1 frame (`6\342\200\22316 ms`) between two `mousemove` events.\n   - Because `stepDirectAngularRate` treated any single frame with `targetRate === 0` as an immediate stop (`effectiveTau = baseTau / 4.5 = 0.44 ms`, snapping `< 0.02 rad/s` to `0`), `yawVelocity` and `pitchVelocity` repeatedly slammed to `0` on every interleaved frame during a continuous physical mouse drag.\n\n3. **Explicit Architectural Separation (`mouseDelta`, `reticlePosition`, `steeringDemand`)**:\n   - In `InputManager.ts`, `consumeSnapshot` still computed a clamped `this.stickX` / `this.stickY` (`[-maxDeflection, +maxDeflection]`) and derived `snapshot.steerYaw` / `snapshot.steerPitch` from those clamped stick coordinates.\n   - In `FlightController.ts`, `this.joystickEval.steerX` / `steerY` (`telemetry.steeringOutputX` / `Y`) were derived from `-this.yawVelocity / effectiveMaxYaw` rather than directly exposing independent `mouseDelta`, bounded `reticlePosition`, and continuous `steeringDemand`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **TypeScript Lint Error (Turn 1, Fixed)**: `src/engine/InputManager.ts` referenced `STEERING_CONFIG.stickSelfCenterRate`, `maxStickDeflection`, `baseMouseSensitivity` and `STEERING_BOUNDS.stickSelfCenterRate`, `maxStickDeflection` which were missing from `src/config/steering.ts`. Fixed by restoring those baseline properties in `src/config/steering.ts` and making `stickSelfCenterRate` and `maxStickDeflection` optional on `VirtualStickParams` in `src/engine/InputManager.ts`.\n- **Playwright Locator Timeout & Stale Dev Server Bundle (Turn 2, Fixed)**:\n  - `button:has-text(\"Launch\")` timed out because the Main Menu button is `\"Campaign Missions\"` first, then `\"Launch\"` on the Mission Select view.\n  - Because Vite HMR is disabled in this environment, code edits did not take effect in the browser until `restart_dev_server` was called. Always call `compile_applet` followed by `restart_dev_server` before running Playwright browser verification.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Dev Server**: Running on `http://localhost:3000`. Remember that HMR is disabled, so `restart_dev_server` must be called after edits before running Playwright tests.\n- **Playwright Browser Testing**: Available via `NODE_PATH=/usr/local/share/bun-global/node_modules bun -e \'import { chromium } from \"playwright\"; ...\'` using `/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1247` with WebGL SwiftShader flags (`--use-gl=angle --use-angle=swiftshader --enable-webgl --ignore-gpu-blocklist`).\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n\n1. **Update `/src/config/steering.ts`**:\n   - Keep `mouseSensitivity: 1.0`, `maxYawRate: 2.6`, `maxPitchRate: 2.25`, `yawRate: 1.0`, `pitchRate: 0.9`, `softSaturationKnee: 0.85` strictly unchanged.\n   - Calibrate `inputNormalizationRange` from `1800` $\\rightarrow$ **`750` px/s** (`12.5 px/frame` at 60 FPS) with `precisionLinearBlend: 0.05` and `responseCurve: 2.15` so that:\n     - Tiny micro-corrections (`1\342\200\2232 px/frame` = `60\342\200\223120 px/s`) remain sub-degree precise (`~1.2\302\260/s to 3.9\302\260/s`, zero fine-aim overshoot).\n     - Sustainable multi-second continuous mouse glides (`5\342\200\22312.5 px/frame` = `300\342\200\223750 px/s`) produce strong, continuous, uninterrupted ship rotation (`23\302\260/s to 144\302\260/s`) before, at, and beyond the visual aim boundary without running out of mousepad or requiring repeated flicks.\n\n2. **Update `/src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts` & `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`**:\n   - Explicitly separate and expose the three independent architectural state structures on `FlightController`:\n     1. `mouseDelta` (`{ x: number; y: number }`): raw Pointer Lock relative mouse movement (`input.mouseDeltaX`, `input.mouseDeltaY`) processed once per frame.\n     2. `reticlePosition` (`{ x: number; y: number; normalizedX: number; normalizedY: number; screenX: number; screenY: number }`): bounded visual HUD reticle position clamped to `this.aimBoundary` via `clampToRoundedRect` (never auto-recentered, never used to compute steering).\n     3. `steeringDemand` (`{ yaw: number; pitch: number; targetYawRate: number; targetPitchRate: number }`): continuous flight-control input computed directly from `mouseDelta` via `evaluateDirectMouseSteering`.\n   - In `MouseResponseCurve.ts` / `FlightController.ts`, handle 1-frame browser event-coalescing gaps during continuous physical mouse drags without introducing angular inertia:\n     - When `mouseDelta` is `0` for a single isolated high-refresh render frame (`< 22 ms` since the last non-zero `mouseDelta`), bridge the polling gap smoothly (`tau \342\211\210 0.018s`) instead of slamming `yawVelocity`/`pitchVelocity` to `0` mid-drag.\n     - Once zero input persists for `>= 22 ms` (the mouse has actually stopped moving), apply fast stop decay (`stopDecayMultiplier: 4.5`) and snap `< 0.02 rad/s` immediately to `0` so stopping the mouse halts rotation crisply with zero drift.\n     - On any direction reversal (`targetRate * currentRate < 0`), immediately clear opposite-sign velocity (`baseCurrent = 0`) so steering reverses on the very first frame.\n\n3. **Update `/src/engine/InputManager.ts` & `/src/config/ships.ts`**:\n   - Ensure `InputManager.consumeSnapshot` processes every raw `movementX`/`movementY` delta once and does not discard or clamp `mouseDeltaX`/`mouseDeltaY` when `stickX`/`stickY` reaches `maxDeflection`.\n   - Bump `SETTINGS_STORAGE_KEY` in `/src/config/ships.ts` to `\'starfall.settings.v9\'` (with fallback migration from `v8` and earlier) so existing browser sessions pick up the updated `responseCurve: 2.15` default while preserving user sensitivity, max turn rates, aim boundary, graphics, audio, and camera preferences.\n\n4. **Compile, Lint, Restart Dev Server, and Run Live Playwright Chromium Verification**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`.\n   - Run `restart_dev_server`.\n   - Execute a Playwright Chromium test against `http://localhost:3000` covering all 7 Acceptance Tests (multi-second continuous rightward yaw movement reaching and continuing past the boundary, immediate leftward reversal without repositioning, multi-second continuous vertical pitch movement reaching and continuing past the top/bottom boundary, immediate vertical reversal, and 1-frame coalescing cadence test) plus fine-aiming stop verification.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow all **Strict Preservation** rules: do not alter Pointer Lock implementation, physical mouse-edge continuity fix, `mouseSensitivity` (`1.0`), `maxYawRate` (`2.6`), `maxPitchRate` (`2.25`), `CameraController`, combat/weapon systems, or HUD layout.\n- Clearly distinguish automated Playwright Chromium verification from physical-mouse human gameplay verification in the final report.\n</summary>"
