  planner_response {
    response: "### Root Cause Diagnosis\n\n1. **Disproportionate Input Normalization Range vs. Visual Reticle Travel (`src/config/steering.ts`)**:\n   - The visual reticle accumulated raw mouse displacement (`1 px/px` at 720p) and reached the `192 px` aim boundary after only `192 px` of physical mouse travel (`~0.35\342\200\2230.5s`).\n   - Meanwhile, `DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG.inputNormalizationRange` was set to **`1800 px/s`** (`30 px/frame` at 60 FPS \342\200\224 a rapid wrist flick) with a steep exponent (`responseCurve = 2.25`).\n   - During a sustainable multi-second continuous mouse glide on a physical mousepad (`200\342\200\223420 px/s`), normalized speed was only `u = 0.11..0.23`, producing just `1.4%\342\200\2234.5%` of max turn rate (`~2\302\260/s\342\200\2236.5\302\260/s`). Once the visual reticle hit the aim boundary and clamped visually, continuing to move the mouse at a steady physical glide speed appeared to stop turning the ship unless the player repeatedly whipped/flicked the mouse above `1200\342\200\2231800 px/s`.\n\n2. **Single-Frame Browser Event-Coalescing Dropouts (`src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`)**:\n   - In real browsers, `mousemove` dispatch cadence does not always align 1:1 with every `requestAnimationFrame` tick during a steady multi-second drag, causing isolated single frames with `mouseDelta = 0`.\n   - `stepDirectAngularRate` treated any single frame with `targetRate === 0` as a hard stop (`effectiveTau = 0.44 ms`, snapping `< 0.02 rad/s` to `0`), intermittently slamming `yawVelocity` and `pitchVelocity` to `0` mid-drag.\n\n3. **Clamped Stick Coupling in `InputManager.consumeSnapshot` (`src/engine/InputManager.ts`)**:\n   - `InputSnapshot.steerYaw` and `InputSnapshot.steerPitch` were previously derived solely from `outStickX` / `outStickY` (which are clamped to `[-maxDeflection, +maxDeflection]`).\n\n---\n\n### Code & Architectural Changes\n\n- **Explicit Separation of `mouseDelta`, `reticlePosition`, and `steeringDemand` (`src/engine/FlightController.ts`)**:\n  - `FlightController.mouseDelta` (`{ x, y }`): Records raw Pointer Lock relative mouse movement consumed once per frame, never gated or discarded when the reticle reaches the boundary.\n  - `FlightController.reticlePosition` (`{ x, y, normalizedX, normalizedY, screenX, screenY }`): Bounded visual HUD reticle position clamped via `clampToRoundedRect` to the rounded-rectangle aim boundary. Never auto-recenters, bounces, or feeds back into steering calculation.\n  - `FlightController.steeringDemand` (`{ yaw, pitch, targetYawRate, targetPitchRate }`): Continuous flight-control input evaluated directly from `mouseDelta` via `evaluateDirectMouseSteering` completely independently of `reticlePosition`.\n- **Continuous Multi-Second Glide Calibration (`src/config/steering.ts`, `src/config/ships.ts`)**:\n  - Calibrated `inputNormalizationRange` from `1800` $\\rightarrow$ `750 px/s` (`12.5 px/frame` at 60 FPS) with `responseCurve: 2.15` and `precisionLinearBlend: 0.05`, while strictly preserving `mouseSensitivity: 1.0`, `maxYawRate: 2.6`, `maxPitchRate: 2.25`, `yawRate: 1.0`, and `pitchRate: 0.9`.\n  - Bumped settings storage key to `starfall.settings.v9` in `src/config/ships.ts` so existing browser storage sessions load the updated calibration while preserving user preferences.\n- **Single-Frame Browser Coalescing Continuity (`src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`, `src/engine/FlightController.ts`)**:\n  - Added `isCoalescingGap` detection (`< 18 ms` single-frame zero-delta tick immediately following active mouse input) to `stepDirectAngularRate` so isolated browser polling gaps do not slam angular velocity to `0` mid-drag, while actual mouse stops decay at `4.5x` rate and snap to `0` with zero drift.\n- **Raw Delta Steering Intent in `InputManager` (`src/engine/InputManager.ts`)**:\n  - Updated `consumeSnapshot` so `snapshot.steerYaw` and `snapshot.steerPitch` evaluate directly from `rawDeltaX` / `rawDeltaY` whenever relative mouse movement is present.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results (Automated Playwright Chromium vs. Physical Mouse Limitation)\n\n> **Distinction Between Automated Browser Testing and Physical Mouse Verification**:\n> The tests below were executed in a live headless **Playwright Chromium** browser (`http://localhost:3000`) dispatching synthetic Pointer Lock `MouseEvent(\'mousemove\', { movementX, movementY })` events into the running application runtime (`InputManager` $\\rightarrow$ `FlightController`). Because this cloud environment does not have a physical hardware mouse attached, physical hand-on-mouse verification cannot be performed directly from the container and should be confirmed by you in the live preview.\n\n| Acceptance Test | Automated Playwright Chromium Result (`1280\303\227720`, 60 Hz) | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1 & 2. Hold continuous rightward movement to & past boundary** (`+7 px/frame` = `420 px/s` for 180 frames / 3.0s) | Reticle reaches right boundary (`reticlePosition.normalizedX = 1.0`) at **Frame 28** (`heading = 20.93\302\260`) and remains clamped at `1.0` through **Frame 180**. | **PASS** |\n| **3. Uninterrupted ship rotation beyond boundary** | Ship rotates continuously from `20.93\302\260` at Frame 28 to **`134.57\302\260`** at Frame 180 at a constant `yawVelocity = -0.7829 rad/s` (`44.86\302\260/s`) before and after the boundary (`stalledFramesAfterBoundary = 0`). | **PASS** |\n| **4 & 5. Immediate steering reversal without repositioning** (`-7 px/frame` left on Frame 181) | On the very first reversal frame, `steeringDemand.yaw` flips from `-0.3011` $\\rightarrow$ **`+0.3011`**, `yawVelocity` flips from `-0.7829` $\\rightarrow$ **`+0.7829 rad/s`**, and `reticlePosition.normalizedX` moves inward from `1.0` $\\rightarrow$ **`0.9635`** (continuing smoothly to `-1.0` and heading `88.96\302\260`). | **PASS** |\n| **6. Vertical pitch continuous movement & reversal** (`-7 px/frame` up for 120 frames, then `+7 px/frame` down) | Reaches top boundary (`normalizedY = -1.0`) at **Frame 18** (`pitch = 10.48\302\260`) and continues pitching smoothly to **`69.87\302\260`** at Frame 120 (`pitchVelocity = +0.6097 rad/s`, `pitchStalledFramesAfterBoundary = 0`). Reversing downward immediately flips `pitchVelocity` to **`-0.6097 rad/s`** on Frame 1. | **PASS** |\n| **7. Bounded visual reticle & zero drift on mouse stop** | Reticle never exceeds `[-1, +1]` normalized boundary coordinates (`reticleNormXHeld = 1.0`), and stopping mouse input halts rotation completely (`yawVelocity = 0`, `pitchVelocity = 0`, `steeringDemand = 0`). | **PASS** |"
    message_id: "10j_aqitB5y0qtsPuZu4uQQ"
    modified_response: "### Root Cause Diagnosis\n\n1. **Disproportionate Input Normalization Range vs. Visual Reticle Travel (`src/config/steering.ts`)**:\n   - The visual reticle accumulated raw mouse displacement (`1 px/px` at 720p) and reached the `192 px` aim boundary after only `192 px` of physical mouse travel (`~0.35\342\200\2230.5s`).\n   - Meanwhile, `DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG.inputNormalizationRange` was set to **`1800 px/s`** (`30 px/frame` at 60 FPS \342\200\224 a rapid wrist flick) with a steep exponent (`responseCurve = 2.25`).\n   - During a sustainable multi-second continuous mouse glide on a physical mousepad (`200\342\200\223420 px/s`), normalized speed was only `u = 0.11..0.23`, producing just `1.4%\342\200\2234.5%` of max turn rate (`~2\302\260/s\342\200\2236.5\302\260/s`). Once the visual reticle hit the aim boundary and clamped visually, continuing to move the mouse at a steady physical glide speed appeared to stop turning the ship unless the player repeatedly whipped/flicked the mouse above `1200\342\200\2231800 px/s`.\n\n2. **Single-Frame Browser Event-Coalescing Dropouts (`src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`)**:\n   - In real browsers, `mousemove` dispatch cadence does not always align 1:1 with every `requestAnimationFrame` tick during a steady multi-second drag, causing isolated single frames with `mouseDelta = 0`.\n   - `stepDirectAngularRate` treated any single frame with `targetRate === 0` as a hard stop (`effectiveTau = 0.44 ms`, snapping `< 0.02 rad/s` to `0`), intermittently slamming `yawVelocity` and `pitchVelocity` to `0` mid-drag.\n\n3. **Clamped Stick Coupling in `InputManager.consumeSnapshot` (`src/engine/InputManager.ts`)**:\n   - `InputSnapshot.steerYaw` and `InputSnapshot.steerPitch` were previously derived solely from `outStickX` / `outStickY` (which are clamped to `[-maxDeflection, +maxDeflection]`).\n\n---\n\n### Code & Architectural Changes\n\n- **Explicit Separation of `mouseDelta`, `reticlePosition`, and `steeringDemand` (`src/engine/FlightController.ts`)**:\n  - `FlightController.mouseDelta` (`{ x, y }`): Records raw Pointer Lock relative mouse movement consumed once per frame, never gated or discarded when the reticle reaches the boundary.\n  - `FlightController.reticlePosition` (`{ x, y, normalizedX, normalizedY, screenX, screenY }`): Bounded visual HUD reticle position clamped via `clampToRoundedRect` to the rounded-rectangle aim boundary. Never auto-recenters, bounces, or feeds back into steering calculation.\n  - `FlightController.steeringDemand` (`{ yaw, pitch, targetYawRate, targetPitchRate }`): Continuous flight-control input evaluated directly from `mouseDelta` via `evaluateDirectMouseSteering` completely independently of `reticlePosition`.\n- **Continuous Multi-Second Glide Calibration (`src/config/steering.ts`, `src/config/ships.ts`)**:\n  - Calibrated `inputNormalizationRange` from `1800` $\\rightarrow$ `750 px/s` (`12.5 px/frame` at 60 FPS) with `responseCurve: 2.15` and `precisionLinearBlend: 0.05`, while strictly preserving `mouseSensitivity: 1.0`, `maxYawRate: 2.6`, `maxPitchRate: 2.25`, `yawRate: 1.0`, and `pitchRate: 0.9`.\n  - Bumped settings storage key to `starfall.settings.v9` in `src/config/ships.ts` so existing browser storage sessions load the updated calibration while preserving user preferences.\n- **Single-Frame Browser Coalescing Continuity (`src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`, `src/engine/FlightController.ts`)**:\n  - Added `isCoalescingGap` detection (`< 18 ms` single-frame zero-delta tick immediately following active mouse input) to `stepDirectAngularRate` so isolated browser polling gaps do not slam angular velocity to `0` mid-drag, while actual mouse stops decay at `4.5x` rate and snap to `0` with zero drift.\n- **Raw Delta Steering Intent in `InputManager` (`src/engine/InputManager.ts`)**:\n  - Updated `consumeSnapshot` so `snapshot.steerYaw` and `snapshot.steerPitch` evaluate directly from `rawDeltaX` / `rawDeltaY` whenever relative mouse movement is present.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results (Automated Playwright Chromium vs. Physical Mouse Limitation)\n\n> **Distinction Between Automated Browser Testing and Physical Mouse Verification**:\n> The tests below were executed in a live headless **Playwright Chromium** browser (`http://localhost:3000`) dispatching synthetic Pointer Lock `MouseEvent(\'mousemove\', { movementX, movementY })` events into the running application runtime (`InputManager` $\\rightarrow$ `FlightController`). Because this cloud environment does not have a physical hardware mouse attached, physical hand-on-mouse verification cannot be performed directly from the container and should be confirmed by you in the live preview.\n\n| Acceptance Test | Automated Playwright Chromium Result (`1280\303\227720`, 60 Hz) | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1 & 2. Hold continuous rightward movement to & past boundary** (`+7 px/frame` = `420 px/s` for 180 frames / 3.0s) | Reticle reaches right boundary (`reticlePosition.normalizedX = 1.0`) at **Frame 28** (`heading = 20.93\302\260`) and remains clamped at `1.0` through **Frame 180**. | **PASS** |\n| **3. Uninterrupted ship rotation beyond boundary** | Ship rotates continuously from `20.93\302\260` at Frame 28 to **`134.57\302\260`** at Frame 180 at a constant `yawVelocity = -0.7829 rad/s` (`44.86\302\260/s`) before and after the boundary (`stalledFramesAfterBoundary = 0`). | **PASS** |\n| **4 & 5. Immediate steering reversal without repositioning** (`-7 px/frame` left on Frame 181) | On the very first reversal frame, `steeringDemand.yaw` flips from `-0.3011` $\\rightarrow$ **`+0.3011`**, `yawVelocity` flips from `-0.7829` $\\rightarrow$ **`+0.7829 rad/s`**, and `reticlePosition.normalizedX` moves inward from `1.0` $\\rightarrow$ **`0.9635`** (continuing smoothly to `-1.0` and heading `88.96\302\260`). | **PASS** |\n| **6. Vertical pitch continuous movement & reversal** (`-7 px/frame` up for 120 frames, then `+7 px/frame` down) | Reaches top bound